rk out what went wrong. Then you name the single line that killed her, and prove it. The demoSeven incidents, about an hour. Free here and in your browser on itch","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-19T17:01:40Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706691491","verified_at":"2026-10-20T22:47:55Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-5120320-1844115010499582","game_id":"steam-5120320","kind":"announcement","title":"A longer guide, a glossary, and a seal you can get wrong","summary":"The guide starts further back nowEverything in this build came from people who played during Programming Fest and told me what went wrong. Thank you. Some of it was hard to read and all of it was useful. If you have never read assembly, there is a longer track that teaches what a program does while it runs: where the machine is, what a jump does, what it means to step. If you have, press TAB and take the short one. On any card, ? opens a glossary of every term the game uses. A wrong seal no long","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-09-20T18:10:10Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1844115010499582","verified_at":"2026-10-20T22:47:55Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"}],"analyses":[],"news_status":{"steam-5120320":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-25T06:40:23Z","status":"ok","all_sources_checked_at":"2026-10-25T06:40:23Z","error_codes":[]}},"news_last_attempt_at":{"steam-5120320":"2026-10-25T06:40:23Z"},"notices":[],"news_sources":{"5120320":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-25T06:40:23Z","last_success_at":"2026-10-25T06:40:23Z","status":"ok","error_codes":[]},"5120330":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-25T06:40:23Z","last_success_at":"2026-10-25T06:40:23Z","status":"ok","error_codes":[]}}}
